15:11.233 --> 15:12.993
[SPEAKER_01]: Jamis recommended him.

15:13.513 --> 15:13.753
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

15:14.874 --> 15:16.934
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, yeah, they're loyal.

15:17.274 --> 15:20.415
[SPEAKER_00]: They're not gonna mess with us.

15:20.675 --> 15:21.136
[SPEAKER_00]: I doubt it.

15:21.516 --> 15:22.996
[SPEAKER_00]: What about Gouge?

15:23.616 --> 15:26.457
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, Gouge, he's fine.

15:26.757 --> 15:29.578
[SPEAKER_00]: He makes quick decisions under pressure.

15:32.459 --> 15:35.040
[SPEAKER_00]: Not much of a threat, though, unless he's threatened upon.

15:35.843 --> 15:36.383
[SPEAKER_00]: Professional.

15:37.004 --> 15:38.785
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, they're pretty professional, I'd say.

15:39.685 --> 15:43.487
[SPEAKER_01]: And what are your feelings of this Jude character?

15:46.989 --> 15:48.490
[SPEAKER_00]: He's a pretty good wizard, you know.

15:49.730 --> 15:54.693
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, the job that you gave him was to protect me, and he did just fine doing that, so...

16:01.156 --> 16:04.678
[SPEAKER_00]: They're very good fighters, though, I will say.

16:08.547 --> 16:12.409
[SPEAKER_01]: So Paul, I do have something to speak with you about.

16:15.871 --> 16:33.162
[SPEAKER_01]: Since you brought to my attention your investigation into your past, your history, your father, I thought on some things.

16:40.694 --> 16:58.591
[SPEAKER_01]: And please think of this conversation as being one of a suggestion regarding your personal career path and how you can be most useful to your family in these times of need.

17:01.053 --> 17:05.758
[SPEAKER_01]: I've noticed that you've dedicated yourself to

17:14.518 --> 17:26.531
[SPEAKER_01]: What could be called Ledger Domain spycraft in a way.

17:28.834 --> 17:30.376
[SPEAKER_01]: And I think that very useful.

17:32.298 --> 17:35.802
[SPEAKER_01]: However, to be honest,

17:37.573 --> 17:49.819
[SPEAKER_01]: When your father, I knew him, I knew Grayson when we were young men and I was very, very impressed by his intelligence and actually the intelligence of your mother as well.

17:49.859 --> 17:51.179
[SPEAKER_01]: They were both brilliant people.

17:58.282 --> 18:03.625
[SPEAKER_01]: He talked often about the yellow substance and how

18:05.950 --> 18:09.351
[SPEAKER_01]: Our state would only be free when we were the ones that produced it.

18:10.011 --> 18:24.676
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know if you know this, but that compound was given to us by the Duke of Berkhoff and he has quit giving.

18:26.057 --> 18:27.137
[SPEAKER_01]: So we're running out.

18:27.637 --> 18:29.298
[SPEAKER_01]: We've been running out for decades.

18:31.259 --> 18:34.740
[SPEAKER_01]: What was left in Helms Island and has been taken

18:35.688 --> 18:41.090
[SPEAKER_01]: It was really only enough to last another three years.

18:41.710 --> 18:42.951
[SPEAKER_01]: We've been desperate for it.

18:43.971 --> 18:46.392
[SPEAKER_01]: But now that it has been removed, we have no time.

18:47.352 --> 18:49.493
[SPEAKER_01]: We have no way to produce that ourselves.

18:49.753 --> 18:51.073
[SPEAKER_01]: We don't have that knowledge.

18:51.954 --> 18:58.616
[SPEAKER_01]: This is what Grayson, maybe two decades ago, recognized and was committed to changing that.

19:04.405 --> 19:10.047
[SPEAKER_01]: Unfortunately, all the greatest alchemists belong to Keoland.

19:13.308 --> 19:14.729
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

19:14.749 --> 19:15.849
[SPEAKER_01]: Or the Duke of Berkhoff.

19:19.370 --> 19:19.770
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

19:19.810 --> 19:20.931
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you know what I'm asking you?

19:21.751 --> 19:26.853
[SPEAKER_01]: To go to either one and figure out if I can find something?

19:28.233 --> 19:32.595
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm asking you because I know you're capable of this.

19:35.361 --> 19:43.407
[SPEAKER_01]: Could you perhaps study the creation of this substance?

19:44.928 --> 19:48.450
[SPEAKER_01]: Could you look into it to seek and quest to figure out a way to do it?

19:50.071 --> 19:50.371
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

19:54.054 --> 19:56.055
[SPEAKER_01]: This would divert you from your main path.

19:59.458 --> 20:02.800
[SPEAKER_01]: And you'd have to delve into the arcane arts.

20:03.829 --> 20:05.010
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you be willing to do that?

20:05.450 --> 20:05.770
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

20:06.691 --> 20:13.416
[SPEAKER_01]: Most Oeridians are reluctant to go there.

20:13.676 --> 20:22.903
[SPEAKER_01]: However, I see now that our negligence of the magical arts have led us to this point.

20:23.924 --> 20:25.485
[SPEAKER_01]: We need to develop wizards.

20:27.766 --> 20:28.227
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, we do.

20:29.508 --> 20:31.109
[SPEAKER_01]: This brings me to my second point.

20:33.262 --> 20:41.404
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you feel like Jude is someone you would be willing to have tutor you?

20:41.804 --> 20:42.064
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh yeah.

20:42.244 --> 20:44.804
[SPEAKER_00]: He's a good wizard.

20:45.304 --> 20:46.845
[SPEAKER_00]: Very, very powerful wizard.

20:47.425 --> 20:48.065
[SPEAKER_00]: He could teach me.

20:49.865 --> 20:50.305
[SPEAKER_01]: Excellent.

20:51.265 --> 20:55.786
[SPEAKER_01]: I've actually asked Lord Jamis to propose that to Jude.

20:55.846 --> 20:58.827
[SPEAKER_01]: From what I understand, Jude is someone that's very transactional.

20:59.610 --> 21:02.151
[SPEAKER_01]: However, right now we have things that he would like.

21:02.731 --> 21:11.813
[SPEAKER_01]: And I think that if he could tutor you in the magical arts and give you the knowledge that he has, it would be very advantageous to our family.

21:13.613 --> 21:21.995
[SPEAKER_01]: And to be honest, having a new prince of Monmurg that has the abilities of a wizard would be very advantageous as well.

21:26.676 --> 21:27.416
[SPEAKER_01]: So I charge you

21:31.838 --> 21:37.362
[SPEAKER_01]: Look into the magical arcane arts, please, as your father did and your mother did before you.

21:39.043 --> 21:42.345
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll give you full leeway in this.

21:42.445 --> 21:50.291
[SPEAKER_01]: You can do whatever you wish as long as it does not bring harm to the city or stigma to our names.

21:51.071 --> 21:58.897
[SPEAKER_01]: There are magics, of course, that are illegal in Keoland, illegal in

22:01.001 --> 22:02.162
[SPEAKER_01]: The Duchy of Berghof.

22:02.582 --> 22:04.784
[SPEAKER_01]: Necromancy comes to mind primarily.

22:06.205 --> 22:17.693
[SPEAKER_01]: But as long as no one knows of it, I'm not going to restrict your knowledge or where you seek knowledge.

22:17.873 --> 22:24.138
[SPEAKER_01]: And you have my full permission to use any resources in the Royal Library to do research.

22:25.818 --> 22:35.786
[SPEAKER_01]: And if there are things that you need to acquire, because I understand wizards have a need for esoteric components, I will do what I can there.

22:36.086 --> 22:41.310
[SPEAKER_01]: The Great Market is visited by wizards world round.

22:42.911 --> 22:52.399
[SPEAKER_01]: And even though we are having a very hard year of it, I assume that we will be able to find in the city, at least right now, things that you will require.

22:53.520 --> 22:53.760
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

22:55.097 --> 23:03.480
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm going to have Jamis talk to Jude about his tutelage of you, but I would like to see that proceed in the next few weeks.

23:05.000 --> 23:05.261
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

23:06.501 --> 23:19.385
[SPEAKER_01]: And I'm giving you and he the charge to figure out this yellowish powder.

23:20.686 --> 23:21.106
[SPEAKER_01]: Gotcha.

23:21.666 --> 23:23.487
[SPEAKER_01]: How to make it, where it comes from.

23:24.367 --> 23:26.068
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything we need to know regarding it.

23:29.791 --> 23:35.975
[SPEAKER_01]: We have months before our supply will run out.

23:38.076 --> 23:42.519
[SPEAKER_01]: Now there are some other locations that we can look into.

23:42.860 --> 23:47.943
[SPEAKER_01]: If Fairwind did indeed betray us, he should have a large amount of that somewhere on Fairwind Island.

23:50.285 --> 23:53.447
[SPEAKER_01]: I do not wish to openly go to war with Fairwind at this point.

23:55.850 --> 23:56.110
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

23:56.130 --> 23:58.391
[SPEAKER_01]: He's a traitor.

24:02.093 --> 24:04.414
[SPEAKER_01]: He's a prince of the principalities.

24:05.515 --> 24:08.656
[SPEAKER_01]: He has a large force of men and ships.

24:08.917 --> 24:09.617
[SPEAKER_01]: So do we.

24:10.637 --> 24:13.659
[SPEAKER_01]: This is true, but we're at war with Gradsul.

24:15.040 --> 24:20.422
[SPEAKER_01]: Right now, showing Gradsul our weakness, our division would be disastrous.

24:20.642 --> 24:22.403
[SPEAKER_01]: So we're going to let Fairwind get away with it?

24:22.523 --> 24:23.324
[SPEAKER_01]: I did not say that.

24:24.562 --> 24:25.403
[SPEAKER_01]: I did not say that.

24:26.303 --> 24:31.987
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that the first thing that I would like to see you and you do is figure out where Fairwind has stored his amount.

24:32.928 --> 24:33.728
[SPEAKER_01]: And then we strike.

24:35.910 --> 24:36.270
[SPEAKER_01]: Got it.

24:39.592 --> 24:41.793
[SPEAKER_01]: He can play his games, we can play ours.

24:43.274 --> 24:46.777
[SPEAKER_01]: But we do have a ticking clock here.

24:47.397 --> 24:50.059
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it will only be so long before we run out and

24:51.003 --> 25:00.108
[SPEAKER_01]: In truth, Monmurg is the most exposed to the sahaugin threat of any of the other holdings of the principalities.

25:01.969 --> 25:02.929
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that makes sense.

25:04.050 --> 25:10.993
[SPEAKER_01]: If the sahaugin could destroy this town, this city, it would only be a matter of time before they reclaim.

25:11.013 --> 25:13.955
[SPEAKER_01]: How long does one barrel put in the water last?

25:16.196 --> 25:16.656
[SPEAKER_01]: Like a week?

25:17.437 --> 25:19.098
[SPEAKER_01]: Not that long, from what I understand.

25:21.480 --> 25:26.244
[SPEAKER_01]: The salting ships would have to go out once every two days with a barrel.

25:26.704 --> 25:29.587
[SPEAKER_01]: But a small barrel covers quite a large range.

25:30.508 --> 25:31.008
[SPEAKER_01]: Miles.

25:31.288 --> 25:34.991
[SPEAKER_01]: And in fact, the entire Strait of Monmurg is covered by just one barrel.

25:35.412 --> 25:42.297
[SPEAKER_01]: Usually what happens is they go up near the scimitars, dump the barrel in the water, and they let the current flow back towards this way.

25:42.938 --> 25:43.799
[SPEAKER_01]: It's been like this for

25:47.990 --> 25:51.611
[SPEAKER_01]: It's been, we've done this for decades now, hundreds of years actually, 150.

25:51.671 --> 25:52.252
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, alright.

25:53.872 --> 26:00.835
[SPEAKER_01]: Alright, I'll get on, I'll start looking into that.

26:01.595 --> 26:02.895
[SPEAKER_01]: Now there's some politics here.

26:03.195 --> 26:10.378
[SPEAKER_01]: This is why I don't want you to yell Fairwind's traitorous nature to the spires yet.

26:11.825 --> 26:20.672
[SPEAKER_01]: What I'm hoping is we can negotiate with him and we can figure out a way to get the supply back or at least for him to give us some.

26:20.692 --> 26:23.674
[SPEAKER_00]: You might want to grab those marines then and tell them.

26:26.916 --> 26:27.237
[SPEAKER_01]: I will.

26:28.418 --> 26:30.739
[SPEAKER_01]: I will have Lord Jamis take care of that.

26:32.481 --> 26:32.741
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

26:36.343 --> 26:36.664
[SPEAKER_01]: Sweet.

26:36.984 --> 26:37.785
[SPEAKER_01]: One way or the other.

26:40.306 --> 26:40.987
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't think they'll

26:42.162 --> 26:43.122
[SPEAKER_01]: They're loyal.

26:43.362 --> 26:46.483
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, they're loyal.

26:46.924 --> 26:47.124
[SPEAKER_01]: Good.

26:48.124 --> 26:48.344
[SPEAKER_01]: Good.

26:49.024 --> 26:52.045
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if I can avoid a war with Fairwind, I would do that.

26:53.526 --> 26:56.447
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want Keoland to see our weakness in that way.

26:56.867 --> 26:59.127
[SPEAKER_01]: We look weak enough to that country as it is.

27:00.608 --> 27:06.930
[SPEAKER_01]: Any kind of weakness between the princes themselves would lead to a direct attack, and I do not want to see that.

27:08.295 --> 27:21.258
[SPEAKER_01]: Another thing is we have looked very weak on the seas and it's because of some magical talisman this king totally seems to have with him.

27:22.878 --> 27:25.638
[SPEAKER_01]: We've lost a few ships when we should not have.

27:26.479 --> 27:33.940
[SPEAKER_01]: And until we figure out exactly what is happening there, I do not want to risk an attack on Keoland's navy.

27:36.116 --> 27:41.018
[SPEAKER_01]: Lord Jamis has some ideas as to what is causing this, and I'll discuss them with you later.

27:41.518 --> 27:57.705
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that actually your arcane abilities, if you have them, will do well in abjuring this advantage that the Toli have as well.

28:00.270 --> 28:08.173
[SPEAKER_01]: Any kind of knowledge you can have with the arcane will help us greatly here, and I want you to be my interpreter into that world.

28:08.953 --> 28:10.173
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't trust anybody else.

28:11.774 --> 28:14.275
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't trust Jude.

28:16.175 --> 28:16.415
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

28:17.416 --> 28:19.937
[SPEAKER_00]: Well... Has he given you enough reason not to do that?

28:19.997 --> 28:20.697
[SPEAKER_01]: No, of course not.

28:21.217 --> 28:23.958
[SPEAKER_01]: But he is not part of my family.

28:32.245 --> 28:34.565
[SPEAKER_01]: I have no reason not to use him as an advisor.

28:37.846 --> 28:40.447
[SPEAKER_01]: I would rather have you be an expert in this.

28:42.027 --> 28:42.847
[SPEAKER_01]: That's understandable.

28:46.448 --> 28:48.768
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I think that would be most powerful, actually.

28:48.788 --> 28:52.069
[SPEAKER_01]: A wizard spy.

28:52.749 --> 28:55.329
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, that's what the times require now.

28:55.929 --> 28:59.170
[SPEAKER_01]: Ship captains and good fighters are not what we need at this point.

29:02.833 --> 29:03.134
[SPEAKER_01]: Awesome.

29:04.795 --> 29:06.435
[SPEAKER_01]: Is there anything you wish to talk to me about?

29:10.798 --> 29:14.700
[SPEAKER_00]: Let me keep those four Marines under my command of my little group.

29:18.422 --> 29:19.443
[SPEAKER_01]: I will consider that.

29:23.425 --> 29:27.327
[SPEAKER_01]: If you wish to remain in contact with them, I can understand that.

29:28.548 --> 29:30.549
[SPEAKER_01]: American Gouge.

29:31.757 --> 29:41.766
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, Merrick is of high rank and Lord Jamis has plans for him, but I'm sure that he can be drawn upon as required.

29:42.026 --> 29:42.386
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course.

29:42.866 --> 29:45.969
[SPEAKER_01]: Gouge is another issue entirely.

29:46.089 --> 29:50.033
[SPEAKER_01]: He's something that Lord Jamis allocates as required.

29:50.973 --> 29:54.877
[SPEAKER_01]: But if there's something, a mission that you think that

29:56.627 --> 30:01.348
[SPEAKER_01]: Would require someone with that skill, then definitely I will allocate it to them.

30:01.448 --> 30:06.470
[SPEAKER_01]: So come to me when you have an actual mission and those four are yours.

30:07.070 --> 30:07.650
[SPEAKER_01]: Absolutely.

30:10.531 --> 30:10.811
[SPEAKER_01]: Sweet.

30:11.491 --> 30:20.373
[SPEAKER_01]: In the meantime, what I suggest is that you and Jude engage in the activities that you were engaging in beforehand.

30:22.071 --> 30:27.413
[SPEAKER_01]: And do research into where and how this powder is created.

30:28.173 --> 30:31.775
[SPEAKER_01]: And also look into where Fairwind may have taken it.

30:34.336 --> 30:46.060
[SPEAKER_01]: This will require spies being sent to Fairwinds Island, maybe hiring informants, things like that.

30:46.680 --> 30:49.601
[SPEAKER_01]: You'll have the money that you need for those things.

30:51.302 --> 30:51.562
[SPEAKER_01]: Gotcha.

30:53.807 --> 30:58.608
[SPEAKER_01]: A good spy master knows how to delegate, so I suggest you learn how to do that.

30:59.508 --> 31:03.049
[SPEAKER_01]: Let your agents bring word to you.

31:03.549 --> 31:06.270
[SPEAKER_01]: Cultivate a web.

31:06.290 --> 31:08.630
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't really have any agents.

31:09.791 --> 31:10.431
[SPEAKER_01]: You can get them.

31:11.771 --> 31:17.032
[SPEAKER_01]: Jamis has told me that Jude actually is pretty adroit at doing this.

31:17.493 --> 31:21.734
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I mean we have one guy, but that was three days ago.

31:21.914 --> 31:22.434
[SPEAKER_01]: Find more.

31:22.774 --> 31:23.214
[SPEAKER_01]: Find more.

31:24.476 --> 31:34.720
[SPEAKER_01]: Names has said that Jude is particularly skilled at bending people to his will through various means.

31:38.541 --> 31:39.601
[SPEAKER_01]: Learn that skill also.

31:45.664 --> 31:46.944
[SPEAKER_01]: Use him as your cutout.

31:49.649 --> 31:50.449
[SPEAKER_01]: Your front man.

31:50.629 --> 31:51.410
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

31:51.710 --> 31:52.950
[SPEAKER_01]: I hear what you're lying down.

31:53.030 --> 31:54.191
[SPEAKER_01]: But tell me what he does.

31:54.471 --> 31:56.131
[SPEAKER_01]: And tell me the agents that you have.

31:56.531 --> 31:58.372
[SPEAKER_01]: And report to me what you learned.

31:58.852 --> 31:59.032
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

32:02.253 --> 32:02.593
[SPEAKER_01]: Excellent.

32:03.314 --> 32:04.894
[SPEAKER_01]: Now I suggest you go get some rest.

32:06.035 --> 32:06.555
[SPEAKER_01]: Will be done.

32:07.515 --> 32:11.216
[SPEAKER_01]: You can meet with Jude tomorrow and discuss your plans.

32:11.576 --> 32:11.957
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course.

32:13.777 --> 32:16.018
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so you're led from the room.

32:18.327 --> 32:21.970
[SPEAKER_00]: And you go back to your room in the evening.

32:24.011 --> 32:25.893
[SPEAKER_01]: Actually pretty happy to be there.

32:30.716 --> 32:36.821
[SPEAKER_01]: You take off your still damp clothes for being dumped into the drink with a giant shark.

32:36.881 --> 32:41.905
[SPEAKER_00]: Or my sizzled clothes from that tower that blasted in flames.

32:42.085 --> 32:42.605
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

32:43.166 --> 32:44.126
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't shoot.

